8. Data management and security requirements
Because the system will contain personal information, attendance records and assessment results, security should be included from the beginning.

I recommend:

HTTPS and SSL for the WordPress website and Telegram webhook.

Secure storage of Telegram bot tokens and API credentials.

Role-based access and administrator authentication.

Regular database backups.

Duplicate participant detection.

Audit logs for attendance and certification changes.

Participant consent and a clear privacy notice.

Defined data retention and deletion procedures.

Public certificate verification that reveals only necessary certificate information.

For Telegram integration, HTTPS is particularly important for webhook-based communication. 

