11. My final strategic recommendation
I see this as an opportunity to create a reusable programme-management tool, not just a Telegram bot.

If implemented properly, the BDS-TMS could eventually support other FC Africa training programmes, including NESO capacity building and enterprise development training.

I would propose three deliverables before development begins:

Business Requirements Document (BRD): Explains what the programme needs and what the system must achieve.

Technical Requirements Document (TRD): Explains the plugins, integrations, database, permissions and development specifications.

System Workflow and Prototype: Shows how participants, trainers and administrators interact with the system.

The most important next step is to produce the BRD. It will give your programme team and any WordPress developer a shared reference, prevent unnecessary development costs and make it easier to evaluate whether the final system meets the programme's requirements.

